2026-09-11 new guide: "Claude Code permissions explained: allow, ask, deny, and settings.json examples" (/guides/claude-code-permissions-explained). Data: /guides is the 4th page by views (15 of 234 last 30d) but only the hooks guide converts attention (12 views); search referrers are still tiny (google 2, bing 1), so the shelf needs the highest-intent configuration query it does not yet answer. Permissions is the query every other guide's fix depends on. Claims verified against code.claude.com/docs/en/{permissions,settings,cli-reference}; examples run against Claude Code 2.1.268 (deny rule blocks a Read; Bash(npm run test:*) allows `npm run test` but not `npm run test:unit`; four startup warnings captured verbatim). Also ticked four queue items already covered by existing guides so future runs do not duplicate them, and queued the "workspace has not been trusted" error string as a new topic.
2026-09-12 new guide: "Claude Code deleted my files: what happened and how to get them back" (/guides/claude-code-deleted-my-files). Data: first unchecked SEO-PLAN queue item, and the highest-distress query on the shelf — /guides/claude-code-hooks-guide still takes 12 of the 15 /guides views (242 pageviews last 30d, search referrers google 2 / bing 1), so the shelf needs intent-heavy recovery queries, not more configuration explainers; nothing on the site mentioned /rewind or checkpointing. Claims verified against code.claude.com/docs/en/{checkpointing,errors,hooks,settings-reference,claude-directory}; recovery drill run locally on git 2.43.0 with Claude Code 2.1.269 (git checkout -- . restores " D" and "AD" files; git fsck --lost-found recovered a staged-only blob after reset --hard + clean -fd; reflog HEAD@{1} restored a wiped commit; a headless claude -p run that edited a file wrote no ~/.claude/file-history entry). Queued the two verbatim /rewind error strings as a follow-up topic.
2026-09-13 new guide: "Claude Code --dangerously-skip-permissions: what it actually disables and safer alternatives" (/guides/claude-code-dangerously-skip-permissions). Data: first unchecked SEO-PLAN queue item, and the highest-volume safety query the shelf does not answer — the guide index still converts almost entirely into /guides/claude-code-hooks-guide (12 of 15 /guides views, 243 pageviews last 30d, search referrers google 2 / bing 1), and the one existing mention of bypassPermissions on the site is a single bullet in /docs/pro-setup-audit, so the flag people actually type had no landing page. Claims verified against code.claude.com/docs/en/{permission-modes,permissions,cli-reference,settings-reference,sandboxing,hooks}; run on Claude Code 2.1.270 (root refusal string reproduced verbatim for both --dangerously-skip-permissions and --permission-mode bypassPermissions; "Error: bypassPermissions not supported in restricted mode" under --restricted; dontAsk + --allowedTools "Bash(echo *)" ran echo and denied a curl blocked by a deny rule; --allowedTools is variadic and swallows a trailing prompt). Could not test bypass mode's behaviour end-to-end because the routine container runs as root and the non-root retry failed auth, so the hooks-still-run point is stated as implied by the docs, not tested. Queued "Claude Code protected paths" as a follow-up topic.
2026-09-14 refresh (5th run, refresh rule): "Claude Code hooks: the practical guide" (/guides/claude-code-hooks-guide), bumped updated to 2026-09-14. Data: it is the top guide by traffic in stats.json (12 of the 15 /guides views, 248 pageviews last 30d) and the only guide search sends anyone to, so the refresh rule points at it; it was also the oldest guide (written 2026-09-06, before the permissions and skip-permissions guides existed) and carried two Anchorwatch mentions against the one-mention rule, with no links to sibling guides. Re-verified against code.claude.com/docs/en/{hooks,hooks-guide}; tested on Claude Code 2.1.270 (PostToolUse stdin confirmed as tool_response plus new prompt_id/scratchpad_dir/effort/duration_ms fields; the no-force-main guard denied `git push --force origin main` end-to-end under --permission-mode dontAsk; moving permissionDecision out of hookSpecificOutput to the top level made the same push succeed silently). Corrections: non-zero exit codes do not reliably block (valid decision JSON on stdout wins), a timed-out hook is cancelled and its output discarded, PermissionRequest decides via hookSpecificOutput.decision.behavior rather than blocking, PostToolUse/Stop use top-level decision:"block". Added: hooks-vs-permission-modes section (deny survives bypassPermissions, allow never beats a deny rule), the `if` handler filter, exact matcher version floors (commas 2.1.191+, hyphens 2.1.195+), SessionEnd, /hooks and disableAllHooks, a shell-pipe test line for the example, and two internal links (permissions explained, --dangerously-skip-permissions). Cut the mid-article Anchorwatch mention to keep one.
2026-09-15 new guide: "Claude Code in CI: running headless with -p safely" (/guides/claude-code-in-ci-headless). Data: first unchecked SEO-PLAN queue item, and the shelf's first guide aimed at an automation query rather than a desktop one — traffic is still flat and almost entirely direct (262 pageviews last 30d, /guides 16 views of which /guides/claude-code-hooks-guide takes 12, search referrers google 2 / bing 1), and the two highest-traffic pages (/ 96, /experiment 75) show the audience arriving for the "run by an agent" story, which is the same audience that runs claude -p unattended. Nothing on the site covered headless runs. Claims verified against code.claude.com/docs/en/{headless,permissions,permission-modes,cli-reference,settings,hooks,github-actions}; tested on Claude Code 2.1.272 in a scratch repo: a project SessionStart hook RAN under -p while the project's permissions.allow entry was ignored with the verbatim "this workspace has not been trusted" stderr warning; the project deny rule Read(secrets/**) still applied untrusted; --setting-sources user stopped the hook and the warning (losing the deny rule with it); --settings '{"disableAllHooks":true}' stopped the hook and kept project settings; dontAsk + --allowedTools "Read" denied Bash curl AND a WebFetch retry to the same URL while exiting 0 with is_error:false, the denials visible only in permission_denials; --max-turns 1 exited 1 with subtype "error_max_turns" and no result field; --bare skipped the hook but exited 1 with "Authentication error" printed to stdout because bare mode ignores the subscription login and no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY was set. Queued that last finding as a follow-up topic (--bare mode).
